{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Joshua, etc., from those who spied out the land.</b> It was necessary to state that they were among the spies, to give a reason for their tearing their garments, for one might say: ״Who are you, Joshua and Caleb, to do such a thing, which none of the great men of Israel did?״ And the reason given is that it was not because they considered themselves greater than all the great men of Israel, but rather because they were among the spies who had spied it out and seen its excellence and arrived at that conviction. Furthermore, by this it is also intended to say that in this tearing of theirs they aimed to startle them, as if to say: Would that they had spied it out and torn their garments over its being despised in the eyes of Israel, thereby refuting the words of those who gave the evil report."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:41.932199885Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}